&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=6452903&amp;amp;buildTypeId=IgniteTests24Java8_RunAll&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;TeamCity &lt;b&gt;--&amp;gt; Run :: All&lt;/b&gt; Results&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17503418" author="xtern" created="Wed, 9 Mar 2022 09:05:58 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Problem description in more details.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The race may happen due to fix made in &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-13867&quot; title=&quot;IgniteCacheTxExpiryPolicyTest.testNearAccess almost stably fails in master&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-13867&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-13867&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br/&gt;
On primary node, after ttl update we broadcasting ttl requests to near entry-readers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Specifically the race may happen between read/update/etc of the cache entry and trying to get entry readers when broadcasting ttl-requests.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Race example in &lt;tt&gt;GridDhtCacheAdapter&lt;/tt&gt; between &lt;tt&gt;updateTtl&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;sendTtlUpdateRequest&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;T1-updateTtl: entry = cache.entryEx(keys.get(i));
(create heap entry)

T2-sendTtlUpdateRequest: entry = ctx.dht().entryExx(key, incomingReq.topologyVersion());
(get existing heap entry)

T1-updateTtl: entry.touch()
(mark entry as obsolete - evict it from the heap)

T2-sendTtlUpdateRequest: readers = entry.readers();
(got a GridCacheEntryRemovedException because T1 marked the entry as obsolete and set the obsolete version to EVICT_VER)
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17503420" author="xtern" created="Wed, 9 Mar 2022 09:08:51 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=alapin&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;alapin&quot;&gt;alapin&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;br/&gt;
could you take a look at the proposed changes?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17504758" author="xtern" created="Fri, 11 Mar 2022 07:16:09 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=alapin&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;alapin&quot;&gt;alapin&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
could you take a look at this small patch, please?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Is it possible to use the proposed approach to getting readers, or should we only get them asynchronously?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17512345" author="alapin" created="Fri, 25 Mar 2022 12:15:14 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=xtern&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;xtern&quot;&gt;xtern&lt;/a&gt; Hi, sorry for the delay. Seems that instead of fixing the race, you&apos;ve just removed error log substituting it with debug one, am I right? It seems confusing to me. Are there any other possible cases to get GridCacheEntryRemovedException without &#160;reading a non-expired entry?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17512435" author="xtern" created="Fri, 25 Mar 2022 15:20:26 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=alapin&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;alapin&quot;&gt;alapin&lt;/a&gt;, thanks for your feedback, I just recently finished researching this part, my previous comment to you refers to a different version of the patch.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;gt; Seems that instead of fixing the race, you&apos;ve just removed error log substituting it with debug one, am I right? &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not quite so - we are fixing the NPE, which interrupts the sending of ttl requests to &quot;other&quot; backups and near-caches. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We can only catch a GridCacheEntryRemovedException when entry is evicting from the heap. Entries with Near-readers are not evicted (see GridCacheMapEntry#evictInterna), so we can just skip such a key.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Issue is still in progress, I&apos;m trying to reproduce this problem (ttl is not updated) on the second backup node (without near cache).&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17513234" author="alapin" created="Mon, 28 Mar 2022 08:22:18 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=xtern&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;xtern&quot;&gt;xtern&lt;/a&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;gt;Not quite so - we are fixing the NPE, which interrupts the sending of ttl requests to &quot;other&quot; backups and near-caches.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;del&gt;Do you mean, that NPE itself isn&apos;t fixed rather iteration over keys is continued with the help of newly added `continue` within catch block? &#1053;owever this doesn&apos;t explain why `U.error` was changed with `log.debug`.&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Got it, I&apos;m ok with proposed change.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
